								<div class="title" id="post-title-2823985">
																		
															</div>
				<div class="info">
					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/quetzhal" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(3079060); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=3079060&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1606552812" alt="Quetzhal" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=3079060)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/quetzhal" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(3079060); return false;" >Quetzhal</a></span> <span class="odate time_1495012081 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">17 May 2017 09:08</span>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-2823985">
									

<p>I like the concept behind this one - it's actually pretty refreshing. A horrible ritual meant to create a hostile monster ends up creating a series of beneficial, albeit deformed pets. That said, there are a number of tone issues (particularly in the dialogue) that lead to my current downvote - I encourage you to keep editing this, however, because it's got potential.</p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;Some&nbsp;examples</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">-&nbsp;Hide&nbsp;examples</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<blockquote>
<p>It involves a number of requisites, most commonly being animal body parts, although on a single occasion a human arm was successfully utilized.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>A human arm is an animal body part - scientifically speaking, there shouldn't be anything particularly special about it. It's also an odd sentence in general. You mention a <em>number</em> of requisites, then only specify animal body parts. I suggest altering the sentence to something along the lines of:</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Each SCP-3624 ritual utilizes a selection of material components as a base, most frequently a variety of freshly severed animal body parts. No pattern has been observed in the components selected for each ritual; practitioners appear to be largely opportunistic. These body parts are then stitched together in a shape that roughly resembles a predatory animal (see Addendum 3624-01 for a breakdown of each observed attempt).</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Though I'm not particularly satisfied with that either. I was staring at it for about half an hour before deciding a suggestion didn't necessarily need to be perfect.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>&quot;They are certainly nutters and they don't know we're here.&quot;</p>
</blockquote>
<p>This dialogue is somewhat unnatural. &quot;They are certainly&quot; is formal, and it's followed immediately by an informal &quot;nutters&quot;, which comes off as jarring at best. This would better fit the tone you're conveying with his words.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>&quot;They're nutters. No way they know we're here.&quot;</p>
</blockquote>
<p>And so on. Unfortunately I don't have the time to be completely comprehensive, but I hope that selection helps, at least.</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>

