			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-2852013">
									

<p>I actually like this article, and it's going to get an upvote from me because I'd like to see it survive and grow but I think there are a few issues here and there that need fixing.</p>
<p>There are still places where the grammar could be improved upon. It's a bit too late where I am now to go back into it immediately, but I'm happy to do so in the near future.</p>
<p>There's mention of made of a &quot;Germanic language&quot; without further identification. Even if it's an extinct Germanic language, such as Gothic, I think the Foundation would be able to identify it. If it's something that is only identifiable as Germanic but doesn't have historical precedent, they might describe it as &quot;heretofore unattested Germanic language,&quot; or something similar. I think the Foundation would either have done their research and identified it, or would make a statement to the effect of &quot;it resembles this and we're still identifying it.&quot;</p>
<p>There are a few other things nagging me about the dialogue, but honestly I don't think I can articulate my gripes well enough to do you any good, so I'll refrain for now. If I think of anything more specific and constructive, I'll bring it up.</p>
<p>All in all, though, I like the bones on this thing, and want to see it continue.</p>

